// The eval set. Gold SQL is authored BY THE DOMAIN OWNER -- only they know that
// "adults with IBD" means these cells of subject_disease_status and this age cutoff.
// Draft against the live schema, correct by hand; the corrected version is truth.
// Target 15-20 questions drawn from REAL research questions, not invented ones.
// At least one MUST be a non-metagenome question (askslm is a search tool, not a
// metagenomics-only tool) so the no-scoping decision is enforced by a test.
//
// WARNING -- the three rows below are UNVERIFIED FORMAT EXAMPLES, not a validated
// eval set. Their gold SQL was written against the real mirror's schema without the
// ability to check actual column values (cell contents of subject_disease_status,
// the real age-cutoff convention, etc.), because that mirror lives only on the lab
// server. They exist to show the file's shape and prove the scorer works -- do not
// treat their scores as a measurement of translator quality. The real 15-20
// questions, with gold SQL verified against live data, are authored by the domain
// owner (the researcher), because only they know which cells and cutoffs the
// English maps to.
{"question": "stool samples from adults with IBD", "gold": {"METALOG_METADATA": "SELECT biosample, sample_alias FROM metalog_metadata WHERE subject_disease_status = 'IBD' AND age_years >= 18"}}
{"question": "healthy controls from Israel", "gold": {"METALOG_METADATA": "SELECT biosample, sample_alias FROM metalog_metadata WHERE subject_disease_status = 'healthy' AND geographic_location = 'Israel'"}}
{"question": "human tumour RNA-seq runs, for viral reads", "gold": {"SRA_METADATA": "SELECT biosample FROM sra_metadata WHERE organism = 'Homo sapiens' AND librarysource = 'TRANSCRIPTOMIC'"}}
{"question": "adults with inflammatory bowel disease, fecal calprotectin measured", "gold": {"SRA_METADATA": "SELECT biosample FROM sra_metadata WHERE bioproject = 'PRJNA1265906' AND json_extract_string(jattr, '$.fecalcalprotectin_run') IS NOT NULL"}, "_note": "verified executable against real mirror by Claude 2026-08-25 (134 rows -- the PRJNA1265906/SRP586738 cohort, real fecalcalprotectin_run values, no literal 'IBD'/'inflammatory bowel disease' text anywhere in its study/sample_name/attributes -- this is the exact case that motivated the concept-embedding-search feature); scientific correctness of the gold SQL's criteria not yet confirmed by researcher"}
{"question": "shotgun metagenomic sequencing of the human gut", "gold": {"SRA_METADATA": "SELECT biosample FROM sra_metadata WHERE librarysource = 'METAGENOMIC' AND organism ILIKE '%gut metagenome%'"}, "_note": "verified executable against real mirror by Claude 2026-08-25 (1,902,942 rows); librarysource enum value confirmed: GENOMIC/METAGENOMIC/VIRAL RNA/TRANSCRIPTOMIC/TRANSCRIPTOMIC SINGLE CELL/OTHER/METATRANSCRIPTOMIC/GENOMIC SINGLE CELL/SYNTHETIC -- AMPLICON is NOT a librarysource value on this mirror, so this case tests the positive shotgun match only, NOT a 16S/amplicon exclusion (the real exclusion column, if any, was never confirmed -- see the design doc's deviation notes); scientific correctness not yet confirmed by researcher"}
